# General Rules - VERA (Healthkathon 2026)

1. Use TypeScript with strict type checking. Never use `any` unless absolutely unavoidable.
2. Maintain documentation integrity. Keep `docs/` (Obsidian Vault format) updated as code evolves.
3. Keep functions focused and small. Follow single-responsibility principles.
4. Security first: Never expose secrets, keys, or passwords.
5. Apply the 12 AI Agent Skills principles:
   - UI/UX Craftsmanship (from taste-skill & ui-ux-pro-max)
   - Zero AI Slop (concise, professional copy)
   - Legal/Compliance awareness for medical data (UU PDP & BPJS)
